<title>UK: Holed gasoline tanker chartered to George E Warren.</title>
<headline>Holed gasoline tanker chartered to George E Warren.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gasoline tanker Bona Fulmar, holed in a collision in the North Sea at the weekend, was under charter to U.S. trader George E. Warren, shipping brokers said.</p>
<p>The tanker was carrying 58,447 tonnes of unleaded gasoline from Belgian Petrofina SA 's Antwerp refinery for delivery into New York Harbour when it collided with the Mexican-registered chemical tanker Teoatl in French waters northeast of the British port of Dover.</p>
<p>Divers worked throughout Sunday to seal a three metre high by four metre wide hole and some 7,000 tonnes of spilled gasoline dispersed.</p>
<p>The Bona Fulmar is owned by Bona Shipping A/S of Norway.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
